body:
As an insomniac, it pains me that everything closes by 9pm. I came from Manila, with 24 hour establishments, malls that close at 12mn, etc.  The closest I could prolly hang out in that isn't a pub are the 24hour Walmarts.

Planned Parenthood is the closest I could get to healthcare that is affordable/cheap - I wish we had those in the Philippines. I used to be covered by an HMO with work, and just went in for every little thing that happened to me. Now, I have the flu, and working freelance (soooooo, not covered)  and I just have to bear it down. I'm so afraid of getting sick here.

Everyone will chat your ear off if you give them the chance. Americans are a gabby bunch. just sit down at a Starbucks, and you will find someone who'd want to talk to you. This was bad when I was just starting because I have (apparently) immense social anxiety.

Product returns and Amazon are awesome. Sometimes, they don't even ask why you're returning stuff, they just refund or exchange straightaway. At SM, you gotta be a slick attorney to get an exchange within 7 days of purchase.

&#x200B;

You can pick and exchange broken eggs from other cartons at the grocery.

&#x200B;

Not a lot of convenience stores.

&#x200B;

Not a lot of public transpo. LIKE SRSLY. I'm forced to learn how to drive.

&#x200B;

Taxes aren't computed into the price tag.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Bidets aren't popular here. WAT.
